   "text": {
    "L1": "A supercell is a number bigger than every neighbour it touches.",
    "L2": "It does not have to be the biggest number in the whole row. It only needs to beat its own neighbours.",
    "L3": "In a line, each child checks only the children standing right next to them.",
    "L4": "For the 135 centimetre child, both neighbours are taller, so the child says 2.",
    "L5": "Now use the same local rule on 12, 30, 25, 26, 40 and 8.",
    "L6": "30 beats 12 and 25, and 40 beats 26 and 8. Those are the supercells.",
    "L7": "Notice that an end cell has only one neighbour. Also, two neighbouring cells cannot both be supercells.",
    "L8": "A puzzle may have many answers or none. Showing why an arrangement is impossible is also solving it."
   },
